  dense self-adjoint form realization, an explicit two-sided `LinearPMap` resolvent at `-μ`, and a
  compact resolvent whenever the form embedding itself is compact.
* `QYM.BoundedSelfAdjointPMapPerturbationExtension` proves the genuine unbounded-operator B1
  theorem: an everywhere-defined bounded self-adjoint perturbation preserves the exact domain,
  self-adjointness, and closedness, with an explicit operator-norm loss in the real lower bound.
* `QYM.FormSmallOperatorPerturbationExtension` realizes the B2/KLMN bridge for actual bounded real
  forms and an actual form embedding.  A transparent relative bound with coefficient `a < 1`
