  data, and compact resolvent; the sharp `a = 1` cancellation boundary is proved by a countermodel.
* `QYM.RCLikeCoerciveFormFriedrichsExtension` removes the real-scalar restriction.  It realifies a
  Hermitian sesquilinear form, recovers the full `RCLike` equation by testing at `v` and `I • v`,
  proves complex linearity by uniqueness, and constructs the dense self-adjoint realization and
  compact genuine resolvent without postulating a complex Lax--Milgram theorem.
* `QYM.UnboundedCompactSpectralMappingExtension` transports genuine `LinearPMap` eigenspaces and
  multiplicities through a compact resolvent, including the resolvent parameter and zero-inverse
  boundary cases, completeness, real eigenvalues, and a multiplicity-safe least off-ground level.
* `QYM.CompactSelfAdjointAwayFromZeroExtension` proves internally that a compact symmetric operator
  has only finitely many point eigenvalues outside every positive ball.  This discharges the former
  away-from-zero supplier and yields the negative-resolvent least-gap theorem without that premise.
* `QYM.MassAbsorptionTruncationCore` proves quantitative coercivity/absorption/domination rules and
