### Compact-resolvent boundary

No compact-resolvent theorem occurs in this file.  Bounded multiplication,
self-adjointness, closed graph, and a positive lower bound make the unscaled
operator boundedly invertible onto a closed range once an inverse is
constructed, but none of those statements makes a resolvent compact on an
infinite-dimensional `L²` space.  A future compact-resolvent result for the
Hamiltonian must come from a compact form-domain embedding for the kinetic
realization, not from this bounded potential term.
-/

