namespace QYM.FullCertification.Mock3FullGreenClosedCovariantDerivativeExtension
















/-!
# Exact Green/Stokes boundary and the genuine eta graph derivative

There are three different objects in this file, and none is identified with
another without a theorem.

1. `EtaGeometry.etaCovariantDerivativeLinear` is the genuine manifold
   derivative `eta^-1 * mfderiv (eta * s)` on the smooth inverse-eta core.
2. `EtaGraph.EtaH1Completion Y` is the closed Hilbert relation obtained by
   closing the actual two-coordinate graph `(s, D_eta s)`.
3. `StokesReduction.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual` is
   the still-missing curvilinear divergence theorem on the finite union of
   Mobius images of the circular-arc modular tile.

Mathlib's `MeasureTheory.Integral.DivergenceTheorem` is a theorem for boxes.
The selected Gamma(2) carrier is not presented to that theorem as a box: its
boundary contains Mobius images of circular arcs.  Applying the box theorem
would therefore additionally require a proved finite curvilinear
decomposition, change of variables with its Jacobian, and oriented-boundary
compatibility.  No such bridge is present in Mathlib or in the supplied
geometry.  The first section below proves that this one residual is *exactly*
equivalent to full compact-flux Stokes; it is not installed as an axiom or as
a field of a certificate structure.

The second section constructs the strongest unconditional closed object
available without that residual.  It is a closed graph relation and a bounded
derivative coordinate on the graph Hilbert space.  It becomes the graph of an
operator over the scalar `L2` coordinate exactly when the scalar projection
is injective.  A vertical-vector theorem records the precise typed failure
mode, so the graph relation cannot be mislabeled as an unbounded `L2`
operator.
-/

/-! ## 1. The curvilinear Stokes theorem is the exact remaining Green input -/

/-- Full compact-flux Stokes is equivalent to the paired-polygon statement.
The forward implication merely forgets the redundant zero-tail premise; the
reverse implication uses the already-proved literal quotient-compact tail
tightness. -/
theorem gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes_iff_pairedPolygonFluxStokes :
    Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.GammaTwoCompactFluxStokes ↔ Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.GammaTwoPairedPolygonFluxStokes := by
  constructor
  · intro hCompact X Y hFlux _hTail hIntegrable
    exact hCompact X Y hFlux hIntegrable
  · exact Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes_of_pairedPolygon

/-- Exact irreducible boundary for full quotient Stokes.  All support,
integrability, paired-side, cusp-cap, corner, velocity, and normal obligations
have already been discharged; the right-hand side is only the curvilinear
divergence-equals-oriented-boundary equality. -/
theorem gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes_iff_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual :
    Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.GammaTwoCompactFluxStokes ↔
      QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual :=
  gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes_iff_pairedPolygonFluxStokes.trans
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.gammaTwoPairedPolygonFluxStokes_iff_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual

/-- Planar nullity of the boundary cannot replace an oriented one-dimensional
boundary integral.  This executable counterexample blocks the most tempting
invalid shortcut around the missing curvilinear theorem. -/
theorem planarNullity_cannot_discharge_orientedBoundaryIntegral :
    ¬ ((volume : Measure ℂ) {z : ℂ | z.im = 0} = 0 →
      (∫ _x in (0 : ℝ)..1, (1 : ℂ)) = 0) :=
  Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.planarNullity_does_not_imply_zeroBoundaryIntegral

/-- The exact curvilinear residual implies the full fixed-phase Petersson
Green identity on every weight in the actual dense smooth tower. -/
theorem physicalGreenIdentity_of_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual
    (hResidual :
      QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual) :
    Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.FixedPhaseClosedOperators.PhysicalGreenIdentity := by
  have hPolygon : Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.GammaTwoPairedPolygonFluxStokes :=
    (QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.gammaTwoPairedPolygonFluxStokes_iff_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual).2
      hResidual
  exact Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.FixedPhaseClosedOperators.physicalGreenIdentity_of_pairedPolygon hPolygon

/-- At one weight, the residual gives the literal dense-core Green identity,
not just a name for it. -/
theorem physicalGreenIdentityAt_of_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual
    (hResidual :
      QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual)
    (n : ℤ) : Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.FixedPhaseClosedOperators.PhysicalGreenIdentityAt n :=
  physicalGreenIdentity_of_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual hResidual n

/-- The actual raising operator on its dense Petersson core is closable once
the one exact curvilinear residual is inhabited. -/
