This file is deliberately an *obstruction and exact-reduction producer*.  It
does not install the missing Stokes equality as a field of a certificate.

The relevant Mathlib theorem is
`MeasureTheory.integral_divergence_prod_Icc_of_hasFDerivAt_of_le`.  Its domain
is literally a product interval `Set.Icc a b`; its conclusion is the sum of
the four coordinate-face integrals.  The more general theorem
`MeasureTheory.integral_divergence_of_hasFDerivAt_off_countable` is likewise
stated only on a rectangular box in `Fin (n + 1) -> Real`.

The selected carrier in this development is instead
`closure G.gammaTwoOpenCarrier`, a finite union of Mobius images of the
standard modular tile.  The existing `G.GammaTwoBoundaryParametrization`
stores only a parameter set, finitely many endpoints, a point map, a target,
and `MapsTo`.  It does not store differentiability, regularity, injectivity,
surjectivity onto the target, a Jordan-domain theorem, an outward orientation,
or an identification with the full topological frontier.  The executable
counterexample below proves that this data type alone does not even force an
embedded parametrization.

Consequently the box theorem cannot be applied to the current carrier merely
by rewriting.  One must prove a finite piecewise-`C^1`/Jordan presentation (or
an equivalent finite box pullback with Jacobians), identify all internal
faces, and prove that its oriented face integral is exactly
`StokesReduction.actualTruncatedTileBoundaryFluxSum`.

There is a second independent firewall.  The residual below is a theorem
about two scalar functions `X Y : UpperHalfPlane -> Complex` and the
inverse-eta fixed-phase matter core.  It has no physical sector, concrete
`U(1)` gauge action, Hodge projection, residual-gauge quotient, or
deck-covariant Coulomb-domain argument.  The presently exported gauge slice
still takes `deckPullback` and `divergence` as parameters.  Thus proving this
scalar residual would close the existing inverse-eta Green tower, but would
not by itself construct a closed covariant derivative on the actual
gauge-fixed Hamiltonian domain.
-/

/-! ## 1. Pointwise form of the sole missing equality -/

/-- The literal high-cutoff bulk-to-boundary equality for one flux and one
cutoff.  No regularity or support premise is hidden in this definition; those
premises occur in the quantified residual below. -/
def ActualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityAt
    (X Y : ℍ → ℂ) (Ycut : ℝ) : Prop :=
  QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualFluxDivergenceIntegral X Y =
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualTruncatedTileBoundaryFluxSum Ycut X Y

/-- Once the already-proved paired-side and horocycle cancellation is used,
the missing bulk-to-boundary equality at a high cutoff is *equivalent* to
vanishing of the bulk divergence integral.  This is an `iff`, not a new
assumption. -/
theorem actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityAt_iff_bulkDivergence_zero
    {X Y : ℍ → ℂ}
    (hFlux : Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.IsSmoothQuotientCompactFlux X Y)
    {Y₀ Ycut : ℝ} (hY₀ : 1 < Y₀)
    (hZero : ∀ z ∈ Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.gammaTwoClosedTileCarrier \
        Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.gammaTwoThreeCuspTruncation Y₀,
      X z = 0 ∧ Y z = 0)
    (hCut : Y₀ < Ycut) :
    ActualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityAt X Y Ycut ↔
      QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualFluxDivergenceIntegral X Y = 0 := by
  have hBoundary :
      QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualTruncatedTileBoundaryFluxSum Ycut X Y = 0 :=
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualTruncatedTileBoundaryFluxSum_eq_zero
      hFlux.2.2.2.2 hZero hY₀ hCut
  simp only [ActualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityAt, hBoundary]

/-- The exact bulk statement left after all constructed boundary pieces have
cancelled.  This is definitionally the same mathematical assertion as full
compact-flux Stokes, but it uses the named concrete bulk integral from the
high-cutoff reduction. -/
def ActualCompactFluxBulkDivergenceZero : Prop :=
  ∀ (X Y : ℍ → ℂ),
    Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.IsSmoothQuotientCompactFlux X Y →
    IntegrableOn
      (fun z => Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.HalfWeightDifferentialOperators.heightC z ^ 2 * (Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.HalfWeightDifferentialOperators.dx X z + Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.HalfWeightDifferentialOperators.dy Y z))
      Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.chosenGammaTwoFundamentalDomain.carrier Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.hyperbolicMeasure →
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualFluxDivergenceIntegral X Y = 0

/-- The named concrete bulk-zero statement is exactly full compact-flux
Stokes. -/
theorem actualCompactFluxBulkDivergenceZero_iff_gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes :
    ActualCompactFluxBulkDivergenceZero ↔ Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.GammaTwoCompactFluxStokes := by
  constructor
  · intro hBulk X Y hFlux hIntegrable
    simpa only [QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualFluxDivergenceIntegral] using
      hBulk X Y hFlux hIntegrable
  · intro hStokes X Y hFlux hIntegrable
    simpa only [QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualFluxDivergenceIntegral] using
      hStokes X Y hFlux hIntegrable

/-- Strongest unconditional exact reduction: the advertised high-cutoff
curvilinear residual is equivalent to vanishing of the concrete bulk integral
for every smooth quotient-compact invariant flux.  Hence no remaining corner,
tail, side-pairing, or horocycle lemma can close the residual; a genuine
bulk-divergence theorem is required. -/
theorem actualHighCutoffResidual_iff_everyCompactFluxBulkDivergence_zero :
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual ↔
      ActualCompactFluxBulkDivergenceZero := by
  calc
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual ↔
        Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.GammaTwoCompactFluxStokes :=
      QYM.FullCertification.Mock3FullGreenClosedCovariantDerivativeExtension.gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes_iff_actualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityResidual.symm
    _ ↔ ActualCompactFluxBulkDivergenceZero :=
      actualCompactFluxBulkDivergenceZero_iff_gammaTwoCompactFluxStokes.symm

/-- Expanded high-cutoff form of the preceding equivalence.  This theorem
pinpoints the missing proof obligation at every admissible cutoff without
using a certificate structure. -/
theorem actualHighCutoffResidual_iff_bulkZero_at_every_admissible_cut :
    QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.ActualHighCutoffDivergenceBoundaryEqualityResidual ↔
      ∀ (X Y : ℍ → ℂ),
        Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGreenBoundary.IsSmoothQuotientCompactFlux X Y →
        ∀ (Y₀ : ℝ), 1 < Y₀ →
          (∀ z ∈ Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.gammaTwoClosedTileCarrier \
              Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.gammaTwoThreeCuspTruncation Y₀,
            X z = 0 ∧ Y z = 0) →
          IntegrableOn
            (fun z => Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.HalfWeightDifferentialOperators.heightC z ^ 2 * (Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.HalfWeightDifferentialOperators.dx X z + Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.HalfWeightDifferentialOperators.dy Y z))
            Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.chosenGammaTwoFundamentalDomain.carrier Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev.GammaTwoQuotientGeometry.hyperbolicMeasure →
          ∀ (Ycut : ℝ), Y₀ < Ycut →
            QYM.FullCertification.P2GreenBoundaryStokesReductionExtension.actualFluxDivergenceIntegral X Y = 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro hResidual X Y hFlux Y₀ hY₀ hZero hIntegrable Ycut hCut
    have hEquality : ActualHighCutoffBoundaryEqualityAt X Y Ycut :=
